- Accounting.
- Accounts Payable.
- Accounts Receivable.
- Debit notes.
- Credit notes.
- Official accounting reports.

Operations supplies verified:
- GRNs.
- Purchase transaction references.
- Inventory movements.
- Material consumption.
- Production output.
- Cost-basis information.
- Dispatch information.
- Supplier return records.

Do not post General Ledger entries from Operations.

## Distribution

Distribution owns:
- Distributor and C&F partner relationships.
- Distribution network management.
- Distributor operations.

Operations handles physical stock movements and warehouse dispatch.

Do not duplicate distributor management.

## HRMS

HRMS owns:
- Employee records.
- Attendance.
- Payroll.
- Employee management.

Operations may reference employee IDs and assigned operators.

Do not create another employee master.

## Field Sales

Field Sales owns GPS and beat tracking.

Operations must not implement GPS tracking.

## Shopify and Marketplaces

Use existing product and SKU mappings.

Do not rebuild marketplace integrations.

